From: cudy-wr3000v2 wifi-transport-port lane
Subject: [NOT FOR BUILD YET] luofu DTS: add dma-ranges so the DWC framework
 programs the RC inbound iATU window (device -> host DRAM)

The Hi5622 endpoints DMA the ETE ring node arrays and message buffers in host
DRAM through the RC inbound window.  Device-side evidence (phase42 E.3,
phase43 [V*]): the ETE channel base registers point into PCI address space
0x80000000..0xffffffff, and the vendor's live DR0 base 0x8490b000 resolves to
host DRAM.  On this board DRAM phys starts at 0x80000000 (DTS memory node
0x80500000), so the window is identity: PCI 0x80000000 -> CPU phys 0x80000000,
size 2 GiB.  The DWC host framework programs one inbound viewport per
dma-ranges entry (dw_pcie_iatu_setup -> dw_pcie_prog_inbound_atu,
pcie-designware-host.c:945 in the 6.18.60 tree).

The 6.18 skeleton module then obtains the device-side buffer addresses from
dma_alloc_coherent() dma handles - exactly the 0x8xxxxxxx values the ETE
engine expects - and must NOT copy the vendor's host-VA == device-address
identity (that was an accident of the vendor's 2 GiB userspace/kernel split;
our 6.18 config is VMSPLIT_3G).

Status: patch kept here as the mapping deliverable; it is NOT applied to
target-skeleton and NOT built yet.  It is a bench prerequisite for stage B2
(ETE rings) only - stage B1 (upload + mailbox + ready checkpoints) needs no
inbound window.  The wifi@0,0 children stay disabled until bring-up.

--- a/target-skeleton/dts/luofu-r116.dts
+++ b/target-skeleton/dts/luofu-r116.dts
@@ -640,6 +640,7 @@
 		reg-names = "dbi", "misc", "config";
 		ranges = <0x02000000 0x0 0x40000000 0x40000000 0x0 0x2000000>,
 			 <0x01000000 0x0 0x48000000 0x48000000 0x0 0x800000>;
+		dma-ranges = <0x02000000 0x0 0x80000000 0x80000000 0x0 0x80000000>;
 		bus-range = <0 0xa>;
 		interrupts = <0 0x3b 4>,
 			     <0 0x45 4>;
@@ -672,6 +672,7 @@
 		reg-names = "dbi", "misc", "config";
 		ranges = <0x02000000 0x0 0x58000000 0x58000000 0x0 0x2000000>,
 			 <0x01000000 0x0 0x60000000 0x60000000 0x0 0x800000>;
+		dma-ranges = <0x02000000 0x0 0x80000000 0x80000000 0x0 0x80000000>;
 		bus-range = <0 0xa>;
 		interrupts = <0 0x3f 4>,
 			     <0 0x46 4>;
